menu "Attendance uplink"

    config SYNC_BATCH_RECORDS
        int "Records one drain sends before it hands the task back"
        default 16
        range 1 256
        help
            A drain holds m_littlefs for its whole run, so a boundless batch
            would block attend_task for as long as the backlog is deep. One
            batch of 16 at QoS 1 is well under a second on a healthy link,
            and a caller that sees ESP_ERR_NOT_FINISHED simply calls again.

    config SYNC_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "How long a record waits for the broker's puback"
        default 5000
        range 500 30000
        help
            Longer than a keepalive round trip on a slow link, short enough
            that a dead broker does not hold the batch for a minute. The
            cursor does not move until this ack arrives (KEHOACH 6.2.6).

endmenu
